<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Celaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1915">1915</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-revolution">Mexican Revolution</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Celaya, in April 1915, was a pair of engagements near Celaya in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanajuato">Guanajuato</a> in which Constitutionalist forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alvaro-obregon">Álvaro Obregón</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pancho-villa">Pancho Villa</a>'s Division of the North. Using trenches, barbed wire and machine guns, Obregón broke repeated cavalry charges and inflicted heavy losses. The defeat ended Villa's bid for national power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-revolution">Mexican Revolution</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-celaya.jpg" alt="Battle of Celaya" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Subido por Tatehuari el 14 de Marzo de 2007 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla_celaya.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
